I am home in my apartment.
It is Saturday evening, but the sun is still shining.
I am getting ready for the bonfire by the beach.
I have packed my bag.
I put a warm sweater in the bag.
I bought the sweater in February.
The evenings are bright now, but it often gets cold later.
I have also made some snacks.
I shopped this morning before my shift at the café.
My phone rings, and I answer it.
It is Eva.
"Are you ready, Maya?" she asks.
"Yes, I am almost ready," I answer.
"I have just found my sunglasses," I say.
"I looked for them for twenty minutes," I laugh.
"Perfect, see you at the water in half an hour," Eva says.
I put on my shoes and put the bag over my shoulder.
I lock the door and walk down the stairs.
I am really looking forward to my first Danish summer evening.
